# From "First Stage Separation" (Wave III - Freedom, CD3-6). Five graduated
# movement exercises at F12, each practicing a different kind of freedom of
# movement, each with its own return to where it began.

@segment  first-stage-separation
@title    First Stage Separation
@levels   F12
@duration ~7m

say Now, practice freedom of movement — so you can move freely, wherever and whenever you desire.
pause 6
say First: imagine turning over, slowly, like a log rolling in water.
pause 8
say Keep rolling, slowly, all the way around.
pause 8
say Now slow down, and stop exactly where you began.
pause 8
say Second: imagine yourself as a long, straight, stiff pole, lying flat. The end that's your head begins to lift.
pause 8
say Slowly tilting upward, more and more, until you're fully upright.
pause 8
say Now tilt back down the way you came, slowly, until you're flat again — and relax. You're no longer the pole.
pause 8
say Third: imagine backing away from where you are right now, slowly and easily.
pause 8
say Keep moving back, until you can see the back of your own head, the back of your body.
pause 8
say Stop, and feel exactly where you are now.
pause 8
say Now return, moving forward slowly, until you can no longer see yourself because you're too close — and now you're back where you started.
pause 10
say Fourth: imagine an opening at the top of your head, and yourself flowing out through it, like a cloud.
pause 8
say Flowing outward, evenly, more and more, until you feel free — free enough to look back and see the top of your head from where you've flowed to.
pause 10
say Now flow back, through the top of your head, slowly and calmly, until you're back exactly where you started.
pause 10
say Fifth: imagine the feeling of floating upward, up and away from where you are.
pause 8
say Floating higher, more and more, until you can look down and see your physical body from where you're hovering.
pause 8
say Now float back down, slowly and calmly, until you're close enough that you can no longer see your body from outside it — you're back.
pause 10
say Relax. Breathe easily. You've returned each time, and you can always return.
pause 8
